---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('attentive')!;
const b = appBySlug('brevo')!;
const path = '/compare/attentive-vs-brevo';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/attentive-vs-brevo');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/attentive-vs-brevo');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When does Brevo fit this comparison?",
    "answer": "When the Shopify connection and permission import can be reconciled and your team can own the resulting recovery queues."
  },
  {
    "question": "What must happen before importing Shopify contacts?",
    "answer": "Preserve suppression evidence and reconcile subscription status changes; Brevo warns that import can overwrite contact attributes, including subscription status."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Attentive email automatically enabled?",
    "answer": "Attentive documents triggered email journeys but instructs merchants to request access; confirm enablement in the selected account."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do these examples prove a winner?",
    "answer": "No. The workflows are proposed acceptance exercises. Compare deduplicated contribution and operator effort with uncertainty before choosing."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16"><div class="container">
<a href="/compare" class="link">← Comparisons</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">{a.name} vs {b.name} for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
<p class="mt-7 text-xl">Permission provenance across the Shopify import: compare permissions, event handoffs and operating cost with your own checkout.</p>
<TldrBox picks={[{label:"Attentive",tool:a.name,reason:"Evaluate email and SMS journeys after confirming channel access."},{label:"Brevo",tool:b.name,reason:"When the Shopify connection and permission import can be reconciled and your team can own the resulting recovery queues."}]} />
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Attentive</th><th>Brevo</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Operating focus</td><td>Email access and channel ownership</td><td>Permission provenance across the Shopify import</td></tr>
<tr><td>Required evidence</td><td>Enabled journey, permission and purchase exit</td><td>Reconcile subscription status before release</td></tr>
<tr><td>Budget</td><td>Current channel and service quote</td><td>Current scope plus handoff and staff costs</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Choose the connection before the channel ladder</h2>
<p>Attentive documents email steps for cart abandonment and Shopify checkout abandonment, with a contact-for-access instruction. Confirm email access before designing a combined journey. <a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408727834772-Emails-in-journeys">Attentive journey documentation</a> establishes capability, not automatic enablement in every account.</p>
<h2>Brevo now connects through Brevo PushOwl</h2>
<p><a href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879-Brevo-PushOwl-app-for-Shopify-Connect-your-Shopify-store-with-Brevo-PushOwl">Brevo’s Shopify connection guide</a> describes Brevo PushOwl and multiple messaging channels. Distinguish that app from an existing direct Brevo account. Confirm which account is linked before import; app installation alone does not demonstrate an eligible recovery audience or a working cart trigger.</p>
<h2>Reconcile subscription status before release</h2>
<p>The same guide warns that importing Shopify data may overwrite existing contact attributes, including subscription status. Preserve the pre-import suppression record and compare it with Shopify permission records on a small test set. Include a previously unsubscribed email, an SMS-only subscriber and a customer with no marketing permission. Explain every changed status before enabling a queued reminder. This is a proposed acceptance exercise, not a completed import test.</p>
<h2>Make the subscription objection a human handoff</h2>
<p>For a cart with a subscription toggle left on, route the question to support with the selected product, cadence and checkout link. The support owner confirms the customer’s intended purchase before marketing resumes. A changed subscription term needs approval; neither an email click nor an SMS opt-in grants it. For an international shipping objection, use the current destination quote rather than a blanket discount.</p>
<h2>Coordinate the queues after permission reconciliation</h2>
<p>If Attentive owns SMS while Brevo owns email, define a shared customer/cart key and assign one owner to release each channel. Demonstrate purchase and opt-out propagation in both directions, including a purchase while a message waits. Re-import the test record and replay its checkout event: neither should restore permission or duplicate a send. If web push is proposed, verify its separate subscription and queue rather than treating it as an automatic fallback.</p>
<h2>Price the actual account arrangement</h2>
<p>Compare the same email volume, SMS destinations and enabled channels. Request the current Attentive scope and Brevo PushOwl billing terms, including any existing direct Brevo subscription. Include import reconciliation and support time. A lower advertised entry price does not establish lower cost for a store maintaining two permission records.</p>
<h2>Keep incentive economics separate from attribution</h2>
<p>Illustrative $163 basket at 38% gross margin: goods cost $101.06, full-price gross profit $61.94. A 14% order-wide code leaves $140.18 revenue and $39.12 gross profit, a $22.82 reduction with unchanged goods cost. Subtract fulfillment, payment, message and return costs before calling the remainder contribution. This arithmetic is not an observed recovery result or a recommended discount cap.</p>
<h2>Cut over with a measurable decision</h2>
<p>Pause competing recovery queues before enabling their replacement. Reconcile purchase, refund, stock and permission state, save a rollback owner and inspect the return link. Choose timing from checkout behavior and local sending constraints. For a feasible randomized no-message comparison, select allocation and duration from traffic and conversion delay. Deduplicate orders across senders and compare contribution per eligible shopper; a platform-attributed order alone does not establish incremental lift.</p>
<p>Primary product scope checked November 25, 2026. The linked documentation establishes the stated scope; the operational exercises above remain proposals for your team.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
</div></section></BaseLayout>
